From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] WinSystemAmlogic: present the frame when the GUI was composited

A frame whose GUI render pass was skipped still writes the back buffer when
HDR GUI compositing is on: EndGuiComposite clears it, and CompositeGui draws
the cached GUI over it.

PresentRender only presented when the GUI pass itself had drawn, so during
fullscreen video with a static GUI that work was discarded every frame, and
the render loop had nothing to pace it.

Present whenever the back buffer was written. The GBM backend already flips
whenever a video layer is up.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
@@ -281,7 +281,9 @@
   }
 
   SetVSync(true);
-  if (rendered)
+  // A frame whose GUI render was skipped still wrote the back buffer when
+  // compositing is on, so it has to be presented like any other.
+  if (rendered || (videoLayer && m_guiCompositing))
   {
 #if defined(EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync) && defined(EGL_KHR_fence_sync)
     if (m_eglFence)
